1189:
(a) Hearings: The planning commission board shall be authorized by the McDuffie County Board of Commissioners to hear applications submitted to its director for variances and appeals from the requirements and administrative procedures of this article. The planning commission shall set the time and place of such hearing and shall post a public notice of the variance or appeal hearing on the effected property.
(b) Variance considerations: Variances will only be issued in cases there, owing to special conditions, a literal enforcement of the provisions of this article will result in unnecessary hardship. Such variances may be granted in individual cases of practical difficulty or unnecessary hardship only upon a finding by the planning commission that all of the following conditions exist:
(1) There are extraordinary and exceptional conditions pertaining to the particular piece of property in question because of its size, shape or topography;
(2) The application of this article to the particular piece of property would create an unnecessary hardship;
(3) Relief, if granted, would not cause substantial detriment to the water quality of Usry Pond or impair the purposes and intent of this article;
(4) The special circumstances surrounding the request for a variance are not the result of acts by the applicant;
(5) The variance is not a request to permit a use of land, buildings or structures that is not permissible in the district involved; and
(6) The variance should not result in an impervious surface of the proposed development greater than 50 percent of the parcel area.
(Ord. of 2-4-98(2), § 11)
